(text "Source: https://www.int03.co.uk/crema/hardware/gamecube/gc-control.html (read 2026-11-05).\nPin numbers are that page's own, viewed looking into the console socket (so a plug is the mirror).\n1 yellow: 5 V supply (used by the rumble motor)\n2 red: DATA, bidirectional, pull-up to 3.43 V\n3 green: ground      4 white: ground (Skillz adapter ties 3 and 4 together)\n5: not connected by the official controller\n6 blue: 3.43 V logic supply (page measured 3.43 V on a PAL console; calls 3.3 V a likely fine choice)\n7 black: cable shield / ground\nThe page's own caveat: pinout is deduced from multimeter and oscilloscope work, no guarantee.\nCross-check: Phob J1 (cable pads) in the Phob sheet = 1 GCC_3.3V, 2 +5V, 3 GCC_DATA, 4-6 GND\n(docs/facts/phobgcc.md, netlist of PhobGCCv2-HW ff645aa). Same four signals, different numbering.\nBridge data pin: GP27 (upstream/gcwireless_bridge @ 5c31147, src/main.cpp line 10)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 40.000 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "ca578f93-39e1-583b-8254-4a423b05af83"))
(embedded_fonts no)
